      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Liberals typically anchor their arguments in **liberal theology** (the \"Liber Theologicus\") and **liberal humanism**, which re-interpret core doctrines to emphasize reason and individual conscience over strict adherence to tradition. Theologically, this often involves a re-reading of the \"defense of the weak\" in the Bible as a mandate to alleviate horrific suffering just as much as securing its avoidance, effectively framing self-determination over death as an act of **pro-wellness** rather than a violation of God's order. Philosophically, they frequently integrate ** Existentialism** and **Kantian ethics**, arguing that the absolute right to self-determination is the ultimate \"echo of God in man,\" and that true dignity (the end in itself) is lost when one is forced to endure a \"withering\" that constitutes a psychological and spiritual as well as physical death.",
